ampaign/scorecard.py", "packages/evals/docs/reading-reports.md", "packages/evals/tests/test_scorecard_baseline.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "Off-page readings of a page's measure still print by the number rule, not the measure's set: rung 5's CLI reads 'Must-fix findings open 0.43' where its page reads '0.4 (0 to 0.9)'", "recommendation": "Class. Rule 1 and rule 5 (the CLI prints the decided text) and \u00a72.3's 'a hundredth is noise at n = 7' apply. 4113acd18 moved only judged scores in the writer eval's readings table to a tenth (`score_readings`). Every other non-rate reading still goes through `PageForms.reading` at `_READING_PLACES = 2` (forms.py, writer_eval.py:704). The re-pinned ladder block shows it: ladder.md:497-500 prints 'Bounces 0.86 / 1.00', 'Must-fix findings open 0.43 / 0.29', 'Should-fix findings open 2.43 / 1.57' and 'Writer turns 12.57 / 12.29'. The same campaign's page, quoted at ladder.md:536, reads Must-fix as '0.4 (0 to 0.9) | 0.3 (0 to 1.0) | -0.1'. A reader comparing the terminal with the report sees one measure at two precisions. The quick print has the same shape. 9d77c9556 moved per-label rates to their interval's precision (`lone_rate`), but `_measured_text` (quick/result.py:986) still prints a measure's rate through `in_unit`, so 'Urgent score: 83.3%' and 'Escalates score: 98.9%' (ladder.md:81-82, test_rung_one_triage.py:113-114) sit beside 'Accuracy: 90%' and whole-percent label rates in one block. Fix: read these off-page figures through the measure's set (or rule 2 at the cases they are over), and pin one literal per surface. Search: `forms.reading(`, `in_unit(` with role='level' in quick/ and harness/.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/harness/writer_eval.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/forms.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/quick/result.py", "packages/evals/docs/ladder.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "The 'one set table per campaign' is three tables plus a claimed equivalence, and the claim fails for judged levels: compared on the written page, 'derived' (ignored) on aspect pages", "recommendation": "Class: the coordinator's unify task (\"Build ONE table per campaign, keyed through campaign_set, and read it from every page\"). After 84d57cde3 removed `stated_widths`, `PageForms.of` (forms.py:452-455) builds its sets from the report input alone. `of_campaign` / `of_aspects` / `of_bundle` (:483, :520, :537) build theirs from the bundles and readings. The comment at :453-454 asserts the written page's intervals hold every compared interval the other pages state. Nothing makes the reverse true, and one provenance contradicts it. `_written_stated` (:3489-3492) counts each judged dimension's per-arm and by-aspect Stat interval as 'compared'. `_bundle_stated` counts the same levels' intervals as 'derived' (mean_interval from sem), so they set no digits on the aspect or code page. Scenario: a judged pass/fail dimension whose arm-level half-width is about 2 points (its contrasts' about 5) reads '91.5%' on the written page and '92%' on its aspect pages. That is one measure in two forms inside one campaign, which is what the set-scope ruling forbids. test_report_forms.py:452 checks aspect against code only, and test_number_policy_toyhost.py:37 checks one measure written against code. Fix: either derive every page's table from one gathered list (same provenance rule for the same figure wherever it is printed), or add a test that, for one campaign, the written, code and aspect forms of every shared measure agree.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/forms.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_report_forms.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "severity": "warning", "title": "A new report-input unit, 'share', reaches hosts and the analyst with no CHANGELOG Hosts line and no entry in the kit's report-input schema", "recommendation": "Instance. 2fe447d3f makes report_input_build.py:739-742 write `unit: \"share\"` (report_input.py:441-452, SHARE_UNIT) for any host measure on 0 to 1 with no unit and no grade. toyhost_doc's capture was re-taken for it. That changes what a stored report input says, and what the writer's tools serve, for every host with such a measure. The folded CHANGELOG C5b Hosts entry does not mention it: no line names the unit or the 0-1 fraction. docs/eval-report-kit/schema/report-input.schema.json still describes Measure.unit as 'usd, pct, ms, s, usd_per_1k, usd_per_1m'. A host or analyst validating or switching on unit meets an undocumented value. Fix: add the unit to the schema's description and a sentence to the C5b Hosts entry.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report_input_build.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report_input.py", "docs/eval-report-kit/schema/report-input.schema.json", "CHANGELOG.md"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "No current test evidence: prawduct-hook test-status reports 'stale: no .test-evidence.json on disk'", "recommendation": "Instance. At a cumulative boundary review the suite's evidence is owed. Run the gate (`./scripts/test.sh evals`, plus `./scripts/test-integration.sh -rs` per CLAUDE.md) on 4ba86453f, so the recorded evidence covers the tree being merged. Include a run with Chromium available, since the reference-page test above only fails there.", "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "severity": "note", "title": "The rung-5 recordings README and the ladder state the old judge cost ($0.66, total $7.56); the recorded judge.jsonl sums to $0.638", "recommendation": "Instance. Answering question 5: the writer turns are untouched (`git diff --stat d942cb9ec..HEAD -- packages/evals/examples/5-writer/` lists only recordings/README.md and recordings/judge.jsonl). The 'Recorded' row's latest clause is true of the file: 112 rows, recorded_at 2026-11-10T01:29-01:32Z, after b23852e2c (01:25) and before 55b569467, all google/gemini-3.8-flash. The row still narrates the 2026-11-08 and 2ac30095f recordings, though no call from either remains in the file. The cost lines were not re-read. README.md:10-11 and ladder.md:540-541 say '$0.66' and '$7.56'. The file's cost_usd sums to 0.638, about $0.64, for a total of about $7.54. writer.py:9's docstring still says '(the judge's calls again 2026-11-08) for $7.56'. Nothing reads these figures, so this changes no action. Either drop the per-recording dollar figure, or pin it with a test that sums judge.jsonl. Rewording would only go stale again.", "files": ["packages/evals/examples/5-writer/recordings/README.md", "packages/evals/docs/ladder.md", "packages/evals/examples/5-writer/writer.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "test_scorecard_baseline's matrix-line assertion says 'its ends signed (number rule 3)' but its regex accepts unsigned ends", "recommendation": "Instance. test_scorecard_baseline.py:192-193 changed `-?` to `[+-]?`, so 'Drawn from -88.0 to 68.5 pts.' still matches. The keyed matrix line ('\u2026 Drawn from \u2026') then has no check that a points scale signs its high end. The single-range glyph lines are pinned exactly in test_presentation_number_forms.py:361/383 and test_presentation_figure_forms.py. Require a sign on a non-zero end (`[+-]\\d` or `0`) so the comment's claim is what the test checks.", "files": ["packages/evals/tests/test_scorecard_baseline.py"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "The 'one table per campaign' is three gatherers that disagree: the written page builds its set table from the report input alone (_written_stated stamps every width 'compared') and skips the guardrail intervals the code and aspect pages count, so one measure can read at different decimals on the written page and its campaign's other pages", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: 84d57cde3 removed the frozen campaign table (ReportInput.stated_widths, added by 0c6edde9f to meet the owner's 'build ONE table per campaign ... read it from every page') on the claim that 'the written page's own intervals hold every compared interval the campaign's pages state', and nothing checks that claim beyond Kairo's pass rate (test_report_forms.py:597-604; Kairo has no guardrails). Which intervals a page 'states' and whether each is compared/pooled/derived is decided three times: forms.py:3444-3495 (_written_stated, from ReportInput, hard-coding provenance 'compared' at :3495), :3729-3749 (_readings_stated: gain, drop and within intervals, aggregates 'pooled'), :3752-3780 (_bundle_stated: contrasts, cell CIs, judged 'derived', guardrail checks 'compared' at :3776-3780). Concrete divergence: the report input carries every guardrail check's interval (report_input_build.py:528-546, ReportInput.guardrails) but _written_stated never reads it, so a campaign whose guardrail interval is the measure's narrowest prints that measure finer on the code and aspect pages (of_campaign/of_aspects include it) than on the written page; likewise the input has no drop_interval and the written page reads a reading's precision/within width only (_reading_width, :3511-3515), where the code page reads gain/drop/within. Under _SET_SCOPE='campaign' the written page's set still holds only its own widths, so the flag reaches it in name only, and the docstrings at :453-456, :3150-3160 (campaign_set: 'Every page reads its sets from its campaign's one table') and :3792-3796 (_measure_sets: 'which the written page, the code page and every aspect page read their decimals from alike') state what the code does not do. Close it by construction: one gatherer per kind of evidence that the written page also passes through (freeze _campaign_stated's output into the input as 0c6edde9f did, or derive the written page's widths from the same stated-interval walk over the input's mirrored fields with provenance decided in one place), plus a property test over every fixture campaign with guardrails and readings that PageForms.of(report_input(b)).measure(k).places equals the aspect/code places for every shared set.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/forms.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report_input_build.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_report_forms.py"], "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Set scope is still decided by which PageForms constructor a caller picks, not only by _SET_SCOPE: aspect_verdict, contrast_rows, build_code_only_report and the quick Result build an aspect's forms with of_bundle (aspect alone, no code readings) beside a campaign page built with of_aspects(bundles, readings)", "recommendation": "Scope: class (search every PageForms.of_bundle call). service.py:1108 lays a campaign's aspect pages out in PageForms.of_aspects(bundle.aspects, readings), so the code page's readings join each aspect's set (test_report_forms.py:519-546 pins that a narrower reading moves the aspect page to a tenth). Other routes over the same aspect build PageForms.of_bundle(bundle), whose table holds that bundle alone: build.py:510-529 aspect_verdict (the listing lead for a one-aspect analysis at build.py:500-506, and quick/result.py:608, whose docstring promises 'The page, its lead, this line and the exit line say one sentence'), build.py:2246-2266 contrast_rows ('read off any page', quick/result.py:678), and build.py:354 build_code_only_report, which quick/result.py:1373-1379 uses for Result.report beside Result.page from campaign_report. Scenario: a quick eval with two candidates, whose code readings' 95% within interval on the pass rate is narrower than the bundle's Holm-corrected trial contrasts and its arms' level intervals: the campaign page prints '-7.6 pts' while the quick line, the listing verdict and Result.report print '-8 pts' for the same change. So design.md:231-232 ('The scope of a set is decided in one place, campaign_set ... changes one line there') is not yet true: flipping _SET_SCOPE to 'page' is one line, but 'campaign' depends on every caller choosing of_aspects with the readings. Make the campaign's forms the only route for an aspect that belongs to a campaign (pass the built forms into aspect_verdict/contrast_rows/Result.report, as build_code_only_report_in_forms already accepts), or have of_bundle refuse to stand in for a campaign aspect, and pin the quick line against the page's fold.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/build.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/quick/result.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/service.py", "packages/evals/docs/design.md"], "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "Host-visible input change with no Hosts line and no schema twin: a host measure on 0 to 1 with no unit now enters the report input with unit 'share' (2fe447d3f), which changes that input's digest and how a bare input's fraction reads", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. report_input_build.py:739-749 writes Measure.unit = SHARE_UNIT ('share') for a descriptor with no unit, no grade and value_range (0, 1), and report_input.py:441-452 documents 'share' as a unit value; figure_keys reads it as a rate. CHANGELOG.md's C5b entry (:67-119) never mentions it: not the new unit value a host writing its own (bare) input can use, nor that a frozen report input for such a campaign now digests differently, so a snapshot id changes and a stored plan's recorded input stops matching (the effect 0c6edde9f's withdrawn stated_widths line spelled out for hosts). The kit's documentation twin, docs/eval-report-kit/schema/report-input.schema.json:706, still lists units 'usd, pct, ms, s, usd_per_1k, usd_per_1m' with no 'share' (test_report_input checks field names and enums, not descriptions, so nothing catches it). Consequence: Discodon's toy-host-style fraction measures move their snapshot ids on the first pin with no line telling the host why, and a host authoring a bare input cannot learn to declare a fraction so it reads 78% rather than 0.78. Add one clause to the C5b Hosts paragraph and the unit to the schema twin's description. Checked and fine: the explicit-digit fmt, CostQualityPoint.pass_rate_text/pass_rate_interval_text, settle level and weakest.interval moving to reads, the kit and static-page joins, interval_text and the signed filter are each covered by that entry; api/surface.json needs no change (CostQualityPoint and TableCell are provisional models with empty signatures, and test_api_surface byte-compares the snapshot), and MIGRATIONS.toml needs none (no public-root name left a root: percent_at, bare_places, respell_bare and rate_columns were never root exports).", "files": ["CHANGELOG.md", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report_input_build.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report_input.py", "docs/eval-report-kit/schema/report-input.schema.json"], "fid": "R-11"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Dead paths the G1 sweep left: the retired whole-percents-per-column rule (charts.percent_places, respell_percents, _percents_by_column, even_precision's percents) has no production caller but stays exported and pinned by tests; MeasureForm.level_decimals/change_decimals are never read; PageForms.level/change take an 'alone' flag that does nothing", "recommendation": "Scope: instance (three sites). (1) charts.py:441-489 implements the 11-07 column rule that number-forms \u00a72.3 retired; after 7bfb9b30d its only production caller of even_precision is _costs_alike (charts.py:1582), which passes money texts that hold no percent, yet even_precision stays in charts.__all__ (:2026) with percents=True by default, and tests pin the retired rule as live: test_analyst_render.py:697-701 ('63 twice: one decimal'), and the _values helper (test_analyst_render.py:141-149) still pads a TableBlock through even_precision 'as block_render reads them', while production analyst/blocks.py:451-470 values_table now prints decided text unpadded, so that test's oracle encodes a transform production no longer does. A maintainer reading either believes a column respell still runs. Delete percent_places/respell_percents/_percents_by_column and the percents parameter, and have the test call values_table. (2) MeasureForm.level_decimals/change_decimals (forms.py:349-350, set =places on the code page and None on the written page) have no reader in src (only test_report_forms.py:790), and the places docstring (:362-364) still says a page 'still spell[s] them by level_decimals and change_decimals': two fields that duplicate places and disagree by page. Drop them. (3) PageForms.level and change (forms.py:1149, :1194) accept alone=..., documented as moving no digit, and ignore it; its one caller is scorecard.py:2015. Remove the parameter.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/charts.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_analyst_render.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/forms.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/campaign/scorecard.py"], "fid": "R-12"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "The joint guarantee is computed in three places although figure_keys.joint_level calls itself 'the one owner': build._family_guarantee and the scorecard's pairs note each compute 1 - alpha, the size and their own size-1 guard", "recommendation": "Scope: class (search FAMILY_LEVEL_TEMPLATE.format). figure_keys.py:732-750 joint_level (written page, ContrastFamily; guards: no alpha, correction none, size < 2) is read by forms.interval_level (forms.py:3315-3333); the aspect page's headings use build.py:1866-1878 _family_guarantee (ComparisonFamily; guard size < 2 or no interval_level), and the code page's pairs note scorecard.py:1495-1499 builds the joint