r_eval.py:682 ('plan \u00a72.3'). This is the class prior R-11 (rev-20261108T130215Z-471c02ef) fixed once; these are new instances, not a re-raise. Here is who goes wrong. A maintainer weighing `_SCORE_HUNDREDTHS_FROM = 30` finds the threshold in no repo document: design.md's 'The policy accepts two costs' says only 'a handful of cases'. Its basis is plan \u00a72.3 line 52 ('reverses O4 below about 30 cases, because a hundredth is noise'), which lives under .prawduct/ (gitignored) in another worktree. A maintainer with a failing Kairo literal test is sent to number-forms-plan.md \u00a72.5, which they cannot open. The Kairo before/after rows now ship in packages/evals/docs/design.md ('What the policy changed'). Fix the instances: point the tests at design.md, the number policy, and state the 30-case reason inline or in design.md. Mechanize the class with an enforcement test over packages/*/src and packages/*/tests that refuses `plan \u00a7N`, a bare `section N.N`, and any file name that `git ls-files` does not track or `git check-ignore` matches (e.g. `number-forms-plan.md`). The existing `GENERATOR \u00a7N` and `ANALYST \u00a7N` citations resolve in-repo and pass.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/forms.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/harness/writer_eval.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_number_policy_written_page.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_report_forms.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_harness_writer_eval.py", "packages/evals/docs/design.md"], "fid": "R-15"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "policy_zero is kept through the G1 sweep with no production caller: a non-underscore helper that exists only for test_number_policy, beyond the reach of test_public_api_has_a_caller", "recommendation": "Scope: instance; the gate's blind spot is a class. forms.py:4366 `policy_zero` came in with C5b-P's 'unused' primitives (2d131792d). The G1 sweep (c932ebf5b..b23852e2c) routed every other primitive into production but kept this one. It has no caller in any src module, its own included. Its only reference is test_number_policy.py:43 and :232-234. That departs from CLAUDE.md ('No public API exists only for a test ... Promote a name only when production code needs it too'), and no decision records keeping it. Production prints an exact zero through `policy_figure` and `policy_rate` (forms.py:4220ff, :4289). So the test's three `policy_zero` assertions pin a helper no page calls: a regression in how a page prints a zero leaves them green, and a maintainer reading `policy_zero` takes it for rule 5's implementation. Delete `policy_zero` and those three assertions; line 235 already holds the production path. Alternatively, route the production zero through it. Why nothing caught it: test_public_api_has_a_caller.py reads a module's `__all__` when it has one, and forms.py's `__all__` (:142) excludes every `policy_*` name. Those names carry no underscore, though, and CLAUDE.md makes the underscore the contract. Of the test-imported names in the span's modules, this is the only one with no src use anywhere. The rest have callers inside their defining module.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/forms.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_number_policy.py"], "fid": "R-16"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "A host's unit-less 0-1 measure now enters the report input as unit 'share' (2fe447d3f), with no CHANGELOG Hosts line and no schema-copy mention: the downstream impact on stored inputs and writer-case re-mints is not evidenced", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. report_input_build.py (_Builder, the `share = not facts.unit and grade is None and facts.value_range == (0.0, 1.0)` line) now writes `unit: \"share\"` (report_input.py:442 SHARE_UNIT) where it wrote null. The report input is a served and stored contract: the analyst's tools read it, and snapshots and writer cases freeze it by content. The C5b CHANGELOG entry's Hosts paragraph covers page text, chart JSON and the CLI, and says 'Nothing stored changes'. It never names this new value of the `unit` vocabulary. docs/eval-report-kit/schema/report-input.schema.json's Measure.unit description (:706) does not list it either. The concrete consequence: writer_bank.py:16-23 documents hosts minting every campaign on a schedule, and refuses a mint whose frozen evidence differs from the live case. A host whose campaign has such a measure would see its next scheduled re-mint refused, with nothing in the release notes saying why; toyhost_doc's capture had to be re-taken for exactly this reason (2fe447d3f). Add one Hosts sentence to the C5b entry: the new unit value, which inputs it changes, and that a host retires and re-mints those cases. Also add `share` to the schema copy's unit description.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report_input_build.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report_input.py", "CHANGELOG.md", "docs/eval-report-kit/schema/report-input.schema.json"], "fid": "R-17"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "Item 7 (CLAUDE.md rules over d942cb9ec..HEAD): underscores, exceptions, module state and fakes are compliant, apart from policy_zero above", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Underscores: an AST scan of every .py file changed in the span finds no `from threetears... import _x`, and no `module._name` outside its defining class. The one private attribute bound across instances, `viewed._issued` (forms.py:1146), and `forms._contrast_places` (of_campaign) are both inside PageForms. There is no `# noqa: SLF001` and no alias. Every new public src name (bar_threshold, reads_undecided, DRAWERS, held_stats, joint_level, MeasureSet, as_printed, lone_rate, of_aspects, rate_readings, recorded, score_readings, share_percent, campaign_set, floor_rate, disclosure_words, SHARE_UNIT) has a production caller. DRAWERS is now public for test_report_kit_contract,